Also please note that this example does not handle possible failures of memory allocation. The C++ standard library does not provide a way to predict the success of `new` calls or any other potential error conditions from allocators, as such errors are generally unrecoverable and should lead to immediate program termination. Therefore, it is highly recommended to always assume that memory allocation may fail, and code accordingly.
