['Here is a high level implementation of such a system in Java using JDK's built-in NIO classes (`SocketChannel` and `ServerSocketChannel`) and `ConcurrentLinkedQueue` for the connection pool management. Please note that this is a simplified example, and real-world applications would require much more sophisticated handling:

```java
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.InetSocketAddress;
import java.nio.channels.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentLinkedQueue;
import java.util.logging.Level;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class ConnectionPool {
    private static final Logger logger = Logger.getLogger(ConnectionPool.class.getName());

    private final ConcurrentLinkedQueue<SocketChannel> pool = new ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>();
    private volatile boolean shutdown = false;
    private Selector selector;
    private InetSocketAddress remoteAddress;

    public ConnectionPool(InetSocketAddress address, int initialSize) {
        this.remoteAddress = address;
        try {
            selector = Selector.open();
            for (int i = 0; i < initialSize; ++i) {
                pool.add(createChannel());
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to initialize connection pool", e);
        }
    }

    private SocketChannel createChannel() throws IOException {
        SocketChannel channel = SocketChannel.open();
        channel.configureBlocking(false);
        channel.connect(remoteAddress);
        channel.register(selector, SelectionKey.OP_CONNECT);
        return channel;
    }

    public synchronized SocketChannel acquire() {
        if (pool.isEmpty()) {
            try {
                pool.add(createChannel());
            } catch (IOException e) {
                logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to create new connection", e);
            }
        }
        return pool.poll();
    }

    public synchronized void release(SocketChannel channel) {
        if (!channel.isConnected()) {
            try {
                channel = createChannel();
            } catch (IOException e) {
                logger.log(Level.SEVERE, "Failed to recreate connection", e);
            }
        }
        pool.offer(channel);
    }

    public synchronized void shutdown() throws IOException {
        shutdown = true;
        for (SocketChannel channel : pool) {
            channel.close();
        }
        selector.wakeup();
    }

    // more methods to handle load balancing, fault tolerance, logging and monitoring...
}
```
This code represents a basic connection pool that creates new connections on demand and reuses them as long as they're healthy. It does not implement load balancing or failover mechanisms for now, which would be needed for high-load conditions.
']

