['Here is a basic implementation of the `DataEncryptionService` class using .NET Standard 2.0 with AES encryption. It uses `AesCryptoServiceProvider` for encryption/decryption, `RNGCryptoServiceProvider` for IV generation and `SHA512Managed` for hashing keys. For the logging service, it is assumed that there exists a `Logger` class with methods `LogInfo` and `LogError`.

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

public class DataEncryptionService {
    private static readonly RandomNumberGenerator _rng = new RNGCryptoServiceProvider();
    private static readonly HashAlgorithm _hashAlgo = SHA512Managed.Create();
    private static readonly int _keySize = 256; // 128, 192, or 256 bits
    private static readonly PaddingMode _paddingMode = PaddingMode.PKCS7;
    private static readonly Logger _logger = new Logger();

    public async Task<byte[]> EncryptAsync(byte[] dataToEncrypt, byte[] key) {
        try {
            using (var aesAlg = CreateAES(_hashAlgo.ComputeHash(key), _keySize)) {
                var iv = GenerateIV();
                using (var encryptor = aesAlg.CreateEncryptor(aesAlg.Key, iv)) {
                    return await TransformAsync(encryptor, dataToEncrypt);
                }
            }
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            _logger.LogError("Encryption error: " + ex.Message);
            throw;
        }
    }

    public async Task<byte[]> DecryptAsync(byte[] dataToDecrypt, byte[] key, byte[] iv) {
        try {
            using (var aesAlg = CreateAES(_hashAlgo.ComputeHash(key), _keySize)) {
                using (var decryptor = aesAlg.CreateDecryptor(aesAlg.Key, iv)) {
                    return await TransformAsync(decryptor, dataToDecrypt);
                }
            }
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            _logger.LogError("Decryption error: " + ex.Message);
            throw;
        }
    }

    private static AesCryptoServiceProvider CreateAES(byte[] key, int keySizeInBits) {
        var aesAlg = new AesCryptoServiceProvider {
            Key = key, 
            Mode = CipherMode.CBC,
            Padding = _paddingMode,
            KeySize = keySizeInBits
        };
        return aesAlg;
    }

    private static byte[] GenerateIV() {
        var iv = new byte[16]; // 128 bits
        _rng.GetBytes(iv);
        return iv;
    }

    private async Task<byte[]> TransformAsync(ICryptoTransform transform, byte[] data) {
        using (var ms = new MemoryStream()) {
            using (var cs = new CryptoStream(ms, transform, CryptoStreamMode.Write)) {
                await cs.WriteAsync(data, 0, data.Length);
            }
            return ms.ToArray();
        }
    }
}
```
This is a basic implementation and it might not cover all possible edge cases or scenarios. For instance, this doesn't manage memory properly; if used intensively it could lead to out of memory exceptions. It also assumes synchronous I/O where asynchronous operations would be more appropriate for production codebase under high load conditions. Additionally, the logging service assumed here is a placeholder and real implementation might vary depending on how you are using external services.
']

