['```cpp
#include <forward_list>
#include <algorithm>
#include <string>

void insertString(std::forward_list<std::string> &fl, int index, const std::string &str, bool caseSensitive) {
    auto compareFunc = [caseSensitive](const std::string &s1, const std::string &s2){ 
        return (caseSensitive ? s1 == s2 : tolower(s1) == tolower(s2)); 
    };

    if(!fl.empty() && index < std::distance(fl.begin(), fl.end()) && index >= 0){
        auto it = fl.begin();
        std::advance(it, index);

        // Check for duplicates before inserting
        if(std::find_if(fl.begin(), fl.end(), [&str, compareFunc](const std::string &s) { 
            return compareFunc(s, str); 
        }) == fl.end()){
            fl.insert_after(it, str);
        }
    } else{
        fl.push_front(str);
    }
}
```
This function inserts a string at the specified index if it is valid and ensures that no duplicate elements are added. If the index is out of bounds or negative, it appends the string to the end of the forward list. The comparison mode can be toggled between case-sensitive and case-insensitive using the `caseSensitive` parameter.

Please note: The function uses a lambda function to compare strings based on the provided boolean. If `caseSensitive` is true, it performs a case-sensitive comparison; otherwise, it converts both strings to lower case before comparing them for equality.
']

