['Here is your C# code for `FindFirstXmlElement` function and Rust code for `CreateDirectoryAndSetEnvVar` function:

C# Code:
```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Text;
using System.Xml;
using System.Xml.XPath;

public class XmlHandler {
    public static XPathNavigator FindFirstXmlElement(string fileName, string elementName) {
        var settings = new XmlReaderSettings();
        settings.DtdProcessing = DtdProcessing.Parse;

        using (var reader = XmlReader.Create(fileName, settings)) {
            XPathDocument doc = new XPathDocument(reader);
            XPathNavigator nav = doc.CreateNavigator();

            // use iterator to handle large XML documents efficiently
            XPathNodeIterator iterator = nav.SelectDescendants(elementName, "", false);
            int count = 0;
            XPathNavigator firstElement = null;

            while (iterator.MoveNext()) {
                if (++count > 1) {
                    throw new InvalidOperationException("Multiple elements with the specified name found.");
                }

                firstElement = iterator.Current;
            }

            if (firstElement == null) {
                throw new InvalidOperationException("No element with the specified name found.");
            }

            return firstElement;
        }
    }
}
```
Rust Code:
```rust
use std::env;
use std::fs::{self, DirEntry};
use std::io::Error as IoError;
use std::path::PathBuf;
use std::sync::OnceLock;
use std::time::Instant;
use log::LevelFilter;
use env_logger;
use lazy_static::lazy_static;
use failure::Fail;
use chrono::prelude::*;

#[derive(Debug, Fail)]
pub enum DirectoryError {
    #[fail(display = "Failed to create directory")]
    CreateDirectoryError(IoError),

    #[fail(display = "Failed to set environment variable")]
    SetEnvVarError(String),
}

lazy_static_mutex_one_time_create_env_logger;

pub fn create_directory_and_set_env_var(dir_name: &str, env_key: &str) -> Result<(), DirectoryError> {
    let now = Instant::now();

    match fs::DirEntry::bind("/")? {
        DirEntry{path} => match path.exists() {
            true => (),

            false => {
                log::warnate(env_key, "Path is invalid. Attempting to create a backup directory.", now);

                let dir = PathBuf::from(&dir_name[..]);
                fs::create_dir(&dir)?;
                env::set_var(env_key, &dir.to_string_lossy().into_owned())?;
            }
        },
    };

    let dir = PathBuf::from(&dir_name[..]);
    fs::create_dir(&dir)?;
    env::set_var(env_key, &dir.to_string_lossy().into_owned())?;

    log::infoate(env_key, "Environment variable set successfully.", now);

    Ok(())
}
```
In this code, the `FindFirstXmlElement` function reads an XML file in a memory-efficient way using XPath and returns the first element matching a specified name. If no element is found or if multiple elements are found with the same name, it throws an `InvalidOperationException`. The Rust `create_directory_and_set_env_var` function creates a directory with a given name and sets an environment variable to its path. It also logs all operations for debugging purposes.
