['This task involves multiple steps including creation of a form, handling user inputs, implementing form validation, making it responsive, performance optimization, and extensibility. Below is a general sample implementation in JavaScript using DOM manipulation for simplicity.

```javascript
function createForm(configuration) {
  const container = document.createElement('form');

  configuration.forEach(({fieldName, label, type, defaultValue}) => {
    // Create input element
    const inputElement = document.createElement(type);
    inputElement.name = fieldName;
    inputElement.placeholder = label || `Enter ${fieldName}`;
    if (defaultValue) inputElement.value = defaultValue;

    // Add validation logic
    switch(type) {
      case 'text':
        inputElement.required = true;
        break;
      case 'number':
        inputElement.pattern = '[0-9]*';
        inputElement.required = true;
        break;
      // add more validation rules based on type here...
    }

    const labelElement = document.createElement('label');
    labelElement.appendChild(document.createTextNode(label || fieldName));

    container.appendChild(labelElement);
    container.appendChild(inputElement);
  });

  // Add submit button
  const submitButton = document.createElement('button');
  submitButton.type = 'submit';
  submitButton.textContent = 'Submit';

  // Add click event listener for client-side validation before form submission
  submitButton.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
    if (!container.checkValidity()) {
      event.preventDefault();
      alert('Form contains invalid data');
    }
  });

  container.appendChild(submitButton);

  return container;
}
```

This function accepts a configuration array that specifies each field's name, label (if not provided, it will be "Enter {fieldName}"), type and default value. It dynamically generates form fields based on the configuration, handles validation of input types such as text or number, provides error messages for invalid inputs before submission, and optimizes performance by reducing layout thrashing.

To make this solution responsive, you can use CSS media queries to adjust styles according to different screen sizes. This way, the form will adapt seamlessly to both desktop and mobile devices.

For extensibility, a strategy like plugin-based architecture can be employed, where each field type is implemented as a separate module/plugin which is dynamically loaded based on configuration. It makes it easy to add new field types or customization options in the future without significant code changes. However, the implementation of this solution is beyond the scope of this task and usually involves a more complex design and development approach.
