['Here is the PHP class as per your requirements:

```php
class RandomStringGenerator {
    private $characterSet;
    private $generatedStrings = array();
    private $expiryTime = 300; // 5 minutes in seconds

    public function __construct($characters) {
        $this->characterSet = $characters;
    }

    public function generateRandomString($length) {
        if (!is_string($this->characterSet)) {
            throw new Exception("Invalid character set!");
        }

        $randomString = '';
        while(!$this->validateRequirements($randomString)) {
            $randomString = $this->generateString($length);
        }

        return $randomString;
    }

    private function generateString($length) {
        $string = '';
        for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
            $index = random_int(0, strlen($this->characterSet) - 1);
            $string .= $this->characterSet[$index];
        }

        $this->checkAndRemoveExpiredStrings();
        $this->generatedStrings[] = array('time' => time(), 'string' => $string);

        return $string;
    }

    private function validateRequirements($string) {
        if (!preg_match('/[A-Z]/', $string)) {
            return false;
        }
        if (!preg_match('/[a-z]/', $string)) {
            return false;
        }
        if (!preg_match('/\\d/', $string)) {
            return false;
        }
        if (!preg_match('/\\W/', $string)) {
            return false;
        }

        foreach ($this->generatedStrings as $genString) {
            if ($genString['string'] === $string) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    private function checkAndRemoveExpiredStrings() {
        $currentTime = time();
        $this->generatedStrings = array_filter($this->generatedStrings, function ($genString) use ($currentTime) {
            return $genString['time'] + $this->expiryTime >= $currentTime;
        });
    }
}
```

The class `RandomStringGenerator` is designed to generate cryptographically secure random strings of specified lengths using a given character set. It ensures each generated string includes at least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, one digit and one special character from the provided set. Additionally, it avoids generating identical strings within a time window (by default 5 minutes).

This class will throw an exception if the supplied character set is invalid. The `generateRandomString` method generates random string with validation for all requirements including unique and non-expired property.
']

