public class DNAAnagramProcessor {
    private static final char[] BASES = {'A', 'T', 'C', 'G'};
    private Map<String, Long> anagramCache = new HashMap<>();  // This would be replaced with a real caching system

    public void processDNASequences(List<String> sequences) {
        for (String seq : sequences) {
            long uniqueAnagramsCount = 0;
            double totalLength = 0.0;

            List<String> anagrams = generateAllAnagrams(seq);
            Map<Character, Integer> baseCounts = new HashMap<>();  // This would be replaced with a real memory management system

            for (String anagram : anagrams) {
                if (!anagramCache.containsKey(anagram)) {
                    uniqueAnagramsCount++;
                    totalLength += anagram.length();

                    for (char base : BASES) {
                        int count = StringUtils.countMatches(anagram, base);
                        baseCounts.put(base, baseCounts.getOrDefault(base, 0) + count);
                    }

                    anagramCache.put(anagram, uniqueAnagramsCount);  // This would be replaced with a real caching system
                } else {
                    uniqueAnagramsCount = anagramCache.get(anagram);  // This would be replaced with a real caching system
                }
            }

            double averageLength = totalLength / uniqueAnagramsCount;
            char[] seqArray = seq.toCharArray();
            int gcCount = 0;
            for (char base : BASES) {
                if (base == 'G' || base == 'C') {
                    gcCount += baseCounts.getOrDefault(base, 0);
                }
            }

            double gcContent = ((double) gcCount / seqArray.length) * 100;
            String category = (gcContent < 30) ? "low" : (gcContent > 70) ? "high" : "medium";

            // This would be replaced with actual logging and metrics tracking mechanism
            System.out.println("Sequence: " + seq);
            System.out.println("Unique Anagrams Count: " + uniqueAnagramsCount);
            System.out.println("Average Length of Anagrams: " + averageLength);
            System.out.println("GC Content Category: " + category);
        }
    }

    private List<String> generateAllAnagrams(String seq) {
        if (seq == null || seq.isEmpty()) return Arrays.asList("");

        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < seq.length(); ++i) {
            char c = seq.charAt(i);
            String remainingStr = seq.substring(0, i) + seq.substring(i + 1);

            List<String> subAnagrams = generateAllAnagrams(remainingStr);
            for (String anagram : subAnagrams) {
                result.add(c + anagram);
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```
The function `processDNASequences` processes each DNA sequence by generating all possible anagrams of the sequence, and then iterating over these to compute statistics such as unique anagrams count, total length of anagrams and GC content. The category (low, medium or high) is determined based on the computed GC content.

The `generateAllAnagrams` method generates all possible permutations for a given string. It's recursive in nature, creating all possible arrangements of characters from the input string by selecting each character as the first character and then generating the anagrams of the remaining string.

Please also note that this code uses `org.apache.commons.lang3.StringUtils` for counting matches in a String. Ensure to include this dependency into your project if you're planning on running it. You can add Apache Commons Lang library to your project by including following maven dependency:
