    keys = allocateMemory(sizeof(long) * numRecords);
    records = allocateMemory(sizeof(Record) * numRecords);
    metadata = allocateMemory(sizeof(Metadata) * numRecords);

    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    for (int i = 0; i < numRecords; ++i) {
        struct Node* newNode = createNode();
        ++metadata[i].accessFrequency;
        metadata[i].size = sizeof(Record) + sizeof(Metadata) + sizeof(struct Node);

        if (head == NULL) {
            head = tail = newNode;
            head->prev = head->next = tail;
            tail->prev = tail->next = head;
        } else {
            newNode->prev = tail;
            newNode->next = head;
            head->prev = tail->next = newNode;
            tail = newNode;
        }
    }

    currentSize += metadata[i].size;
    ++currentSize;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);

    return head;
}
```
The above code block creates a circular doubly linked list of nodes and populates the arrays for keys, records and metadatas. It also ensures thread safety using mutex locking mechanism.

For memory management, it uses jemalloc library which provides mmap() like interface for allocating huge blocks of memory to reduce fragmentation and improve performance. The memory pool is maintained by atomic operations and logging functions from jemalloc library. 

