['Here is a simple implementation in C language using a doubly circular linked list to store key-value pairs. Note that this example does not handle system dependencies, performance constraints, scalability, error handling, resource limits, or integration challenges. Also, it's assumed that you are working with some sort of API which can return the data based on keys. This is a very basic implementation and doesn't cover all possible edge cases or scenarios.

